-- title:
--   Hecke–diamond ring of J₁(M) embeds into End_ℂS₂(Γ₁(M))
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number with $M \neq 0$. Write $J =$ `JOne M` for the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field `x1FunctionFieldBar M`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let `heckeDiamondGenBar M` be the family of $\mathbb Z$-linear endomorphisms of $J$ indexed by $\mathrm{Primes} \sqcup \mathbb N$ whose value at a prime $\ell$ is `heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ` (the $\mathbb Z$-linear endomorphism underlying `heckeOperatorOneAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and whose value at $d \in \mathbb N$ is `diamondOneBar M d` (the endomorphism given by the action on $J$ of the semilinear automorphism attached to the algebra automorphism `diamondAutBar M d`). Assume `HeckeDiamondInputsAll M`: for every prime $\ell$ the hypotheses `HeckeInputsOneAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ hold for $(M,\ell)$, and for every $d$ coprime to $M$ there is a $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism of `x1FunctionField M` satisfying `IsDiamondAut M d`, together with a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of `x1FunctionFieldBar M` which restricts, through the coefficient embedding, to `diamondAut M d`. Assume also `HeckeDiamondCommuteBar M`: the endomorphisms `heckeDiamondGenBar M i` commute pairwise. Then there exists an injective ring homomorphism $\Phi$ from the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Z}(J)$ generated by the range of `heckeDiamondGenBar M` into $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_1(M))$ (weight $2$ cusp forms) such that $\Phi$ sends `heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ` to [`CuspForm.heckeTLinOne 2`](def/CuspForm_Gamma1HeckeOperators.html#L652) for every prime $\ell \nmid M$, and sends `diamondOneBar M d` to [`CuspForm.diamondLinOne M 2 d`](def/CuspForm_Gamma1HeckeOperators.html#L592) for every $d$ coprime to $M$. Here `heckeTLinOne` is $f \mapsto \sum_{j<\ell} f\mid_2\begin{pmatrix}1&j\\0&\ell\end{pmatrix} + (\langle \ell\rangle f)\mid_2\begin{pmatrix}\ell&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, and `diamondLinOne M 2 d` is slashing by a chosen $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ with lower-right entry congruent to $d$ modulo $M$ (the identity if no such $\gamma$ exists). Nothing is asserted about $\Phi$ on `heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ` for $\ell \mid M$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura compatibility between the Hecke–diamond action on the Jacobian of $X_1(M)$ in its divisor-class incarnation and the classical action on weight two cusp forms: any integral relation among the $T_\ell$ and $\langle d\rangle_*$ holding on $J_1(M)(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ holds among the corresponding operators on $S_2(\Gamma_1(M))$, and conversely by injectivity. It is used to transfer eigenform data from $S_2(\Gamma_1(M))$ to $J_1(M)$ and its Tate modules, in particular by the construction of a ring homomorphism out of the rational Hecke algebra attached to an eigenform and by the statement producing separable annihilating relations on $J_1(M)$.
